<title>SOUTH KOREA: BOK sells dollars at 880.00 to slow won's fall.</title>
<headline>BOK sells dollars at 880.00 to slow won's fall.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea was seen selling dollars at the opening level of 880.00 won in the interbank market early Tuesday to support the domestic currency, dealers said.</p>
<p>The won rose to 879.90 shortly after the intervention.</p>
<p>The central bank has refused to confirm or deny that it intervenes in the market.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
